i1_sdo3  we need to configure these pins' iomux mode via the GRF register when use multi channel playback/capture.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52172 TEST=can assign and switch multiple channels  Signed-off-by: Sugar Zhang &lt;sugar.zhang@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org broonie/sound.git topic/rockchip commit 170abcaae8bec0a53f2f7708a83119ec42fb09e2)  Change-Id: I72261c9ea91229a6786f5b23a01d118b26272126 Signed-off-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349403 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="349403" owner_email="zhengxing@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/03/349403/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I77c49150beee87b945ba770653fa1cb9055dce22" commit="5a2f129972d154c4b921fe4a9a43ec760b4a918a" commit_message="UPSTREAM drm/dp/mst: make sure mst_primary mstb is valid in work function  This validates the mst_primary under the lock, and then calls into the check and send function. This makes the code a lot easier to understand the locking rules in.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org Signed-off-by: Dave Airlie &lt;airlied@redhat.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53350 TEST=Hotplug HDMI monitor into a Acer USB_C MST hub. Confirm kernel does  not crash.  (cherry picked from commit 9254ec496a1dbdddeab50021a8138dc627a8166a) Signed-off-by: Clint Taylor &lt;clinton.a.taylor@intel.com&gt;  Change-Id: I77c49150beee87b945ba770653fa1cb9055dce22 Reviewed-on: https://